摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"An always-on-top notch for DeepSeek Harness that shows which sessions are working, which need you, and which are done. Windows.","id":"gh:1428830416","install_available":true,"language":"C#","name":"dsh-agents-notch","slug":"iArxic/dsh-agents-notch","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","notch","overlay","plugin","session-monitor","windows","wpf"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"An always-on-top notch for DeepSeek Harness that shows which sessions are working, which need you, a"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"nd which are done. Windows."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"**An always-on-top notch for DeepSeek Harness\nthat answers one question: which of my sessions needs "},{"id":"p2s2","text":"top notch for DeepSeek Harness\nthat answers one question: which of my sessions needs me right now?**"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Install · What it shows · Configure · Limits · Develop · 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Recorded from the window itself (--record), frame by frame — not a mock-up."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Why"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"If you run more than a couple of sessions, finding out whether anything is waiting on you costs a\nco"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ntext switch every time:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"| what you do today | what it costs |"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| alt-tab between windows and read each sidebar | the thing you were doing, every time |\n| wait for "},{"id":"p8s2","text":"a desktop notification | one per session, and none of them say which one is *blocked* |\n| leave the "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"sidebar visible | it is only visible when the app is in front — which is when you do not need it |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"The notch is a small always-on-top tab that **never takes focus**, **hides under a full-screen app**"},{"id":"p9s2","text":", and\nshows the one thing the sidebar cannot while you are in another window: **a session stuck on y"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"ou**. When\none gets stuck, the tab grows into an alert that says why, with an **Open** button that s"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"witches the app\nto that session — from wherever it is, minimized or in the tray. And it **never gets"},{"id":"p9s5","text":" in the way**:\npass over it and it fades and lets your click through; rest on it and the board unfol"},{"id":"p9s6","text":" the way**:\npass over it and it fades and lets your click through; rest on it and the board unfolds."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## What it shows"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"That strip is the whole visual language. **Working** wears a slow blue arc and nothing else, because"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"\nworking is the quiet default — and while any session is running a tool, light runs along the tab's "},{"id":"p11s3","text":"lower\nedge. **Needs you** wears amber, **done** green, **failed** red. Every session keeps its own c"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"olour on the\nbot's rim, so three sessions read as three sessions rather than three copies of one."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### It never gets in the way"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The tab sits where you reach for tabs and title bars, so it steps aside. A pointer **passing over** "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"it\nturns it into a faint ghost that clicks go straight through — to the browser tab or the menu unde"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"r it.\nOnly a pointer that **rests** there for 1.6 s unfolds the board, and pushing it against the to"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"p edge of\nthe screen opens it at once. All three are settings (`hoverMode`, `holdMs`, `topEdgeOpens`"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"); `open`\nbrings back unfold-on-hover."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### The tab speaks up"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"When something **new** happens — a session asks for you, fails, or finishes — the tab grows into an\n"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"alert for a few seconds and then folds back. **Open** takes you straight to that session. Only fresh"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"\nevents are announced: a question that has been waiting for an hour is on the board, not in your fac"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"vents are announced: a question that has been waiting for an hour is on the board, not in your face."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### The board"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Rest the pointer on the tab, or push it against the top of the screen, and the board unfolds. At the"},{"id":"p17s2","text":" top is the session that **changed most recently**, so a\nfinish or a question is what you see first:"},{"id":"p17s3","text":" its title, its project and age, how full its context is, and\none line of what it is doing — the too"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"l it is running and the step, the question it is asking in full,\nor how it ended. Below it, every ot"},{"id":"p17s5","text":"her session in one list: what it is doing in a word and how long ago.\nMore sessions than fit? The li"},{"id":"p17s6","text":" in one list: what it is doing in a word and how long ago.\nMore sessions than fit? The list scrolls."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"**Click** a row to put that session on the big bot. **Double-click** a row, or press **Open ↗**, and"},{"id":"p18s2","text":" the\napp switches to it. A finished or failed row has a **✕** that closes it out — the same as ticki"},{"id":"p18s3","text":" to it. A finished or failed row has a **✕** that closes it out — the same as ticking it in\nthe app."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### Sixteen faces"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"The bot's face is the state, read closer. A working bot is **focused** in a tool and **thinking** be"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"tween\ntools, **determined** on a long busy turn and **tired** after half an hour; it is **confused**"},{"id":"p20s3","text":" when a tool\njust failed and **dizzy** when they keep failing. It **pleads** when it needs you, squi"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"nts `^^` when it is\ndone, and falls **asleep** when the host goes quiet. It blinks, follows your poi"},{"id":"p20s5","text":"nter with its eyes, and\nplays a short motion on each change — once, and then it rests. A board that "},{"id":"p20s6","text":"keeps celebrating something\nthat finished an hour ago is noise."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"**🫥 Never in the way**"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Never takes focus, and steps aside when you pass over it: it fades and your click goes through.\nNo s"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"hadow on your desktop. Hides under a full-screen app."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"**↗️ Open goes there**"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Open, or a double-click, switches DeepSeek Harness to that session and brings it to the front — out "},{"id":"p24s2","text":"of\nthe taskbar or the tray."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"**📏 Honest numbers**"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- **Windows 10/11, x64.** The window is WPF and Win32 (topmost, no-activate, fullscreen detection):\n"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"there is no macOS or Linux build. `package.json` declares `\"os\": [\"win32\"]`.\n- **DeepSeek Harness.**"},{"id":"p28s3","text":" Built and verified on **0.2.1-rc.2**. The host half reads `session/event`\n(`{ global: true }`), `ct"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"x.webServer`, `ctx.agents` and `sessionQuery`, and the in-app half uses\n`uiWorkspace`; an older buil"},{"id":"p28s5","text":"d may lack one. Nothing is checked before mounting — see\n*Limits*.\n- **Node ≥ 22** for the plugin. *"},{"id":"p28s6","text":"*No .NET runtime**: the released window is self-contained.\n- Optional: the **`session-finished`** pl"},{"id":"p28s7","text":"ugin, which is what retires a finished row\n(*What earns a row*)."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## What earns a row"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"A session is on the board because **something happened to it**: it is working, it is blocked on an\na"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"pproval or a question, it failed, or it finished and you have not closed it out. Merely being open\nn"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"ever earns a row, however many sessions are attached."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"Finished and failed rows do not expire on a timer. They leave when the harness's own close-out\nverdi"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"ct says so — the ✓ that the **`session-finished`** plugin puts in the sidebar, read over that\nplugin"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"'s HTTP route, or the ✕ on the row. If that plugin is not installed, this one notices after three\nfa"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"iled probes and retires settled rows after 15 minutes instead, and says so in its report\n(`host-repo"},{"id":"p31s5","text":" and retires settled rows after 15 minutes instead, and says so in its report\n(`host-report.jsonl`)."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"When the host stops answering, the board stops pretending — the tab goes grey, the bot falls asleep,"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"\nand the sub line dates the last heartbeat instead of repeating a summary nobody is updating:"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
